sentences.l:
Not to Tydeus indeed was it dear thus to keep cowering,
but far in front of his dear companions to fight with the enemy,
as they said who saw him toiling;

And they, enraged, the Cadmeans, goaders of horses,
back again, as he came up, a solid ambush set, leading
young men, fifty;

We even the seat of Thebes took, the seven-gated,
having led a scantier people under a stronger wall,
obeying the portents of the gods and the help of Zeus;

on the open-sea first it arms itself, but then
on dry land breaking it roars greatly, and around the capes
being arched it rises to a peak, and spits out the spray of the sea;

while the others hushed went, nor would you say
that so great a people followed, having a voice in their chests,
in silence, fearing the order-givers;

And when indeed to one place coming together they came,
they dashed together hides, and spears, and the might of men
in bronze breastplates;

And as when winter-flowing torrents, rivers down the mountains flowing,
into a glen-meeting the two throw together their mighty water
from great springs, inside a hollow ravine,
and of them far off the crash in the mountains hears a shepherd;
